  "note": "Election of the three aldermen for six years (those elected in 1949 retired). Sixteen candidates were nominated on Wednesday 4 May for the fifteen seats, fifteen of them by the Unionist Party: \"Three outgoing members will be returned unopposed as Aldermen.\" Aldermen J. Twyble and W. H. Fairley did not seek re-election; Mitchell and Wright had been councillors."
